            <ArticleTitle>Coronary bifurcation stenting using dedicated bifurcation stents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>105-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report three cases of successful implantation of three different stents specially designed for bifurcation lesions, guided by intracoronary ultrasound. The BARD and AVE are true bifurcated stents for side-branch access and the NIR-Side Royal is a single modified NIR stent with an aperture to allow provisional bifurcation stenting. These designs introduce a new era in percutaneous management of coronary bifurcation lesions. Cathet. Cardiovasc. Intervent. 49:105-111, 2000.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright 2000 Wiley-Liss, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
